    "end": "Mick lost an eyebrow. Worth it.",
    "caption": "Mick, on the left, has just been nice.\n\nAsh: 1.9 million people, a 26-hour day, no moons, and so much static in the air that a kind word throws sparks. A small one crackles. A proper one, the kind you say a handful of times in a life, sets the hillside alight and brings out the fire brigade. So people here talk about the weather. Mick and Tony are brothers, and have managed a whole life on football and insults. Then Tony became a dad.\n\nI told the hotel receptionist I loved the view. They evacuated the lobby.\n\n(On Earth, a static shock you can feel takes about three thousand volts, and one you can see takes several thousand more. The meters on Ash melt before anyone can measure a proper 'I'm proud of you'.)\n\nWhat's the kindest thing you've never said?"
  },
  "first_comment": "The baby has her dad's eyes and, so far, both eyebrows.",
